1	//! The spend ledger (M5 follow-on): an append-only record of transferred
2	//! bytes with a **monotonic period counter** as the only accounting
3	//! authority. Timestamps ride along as human reference and are consulted by
4	//! no query — the corpus rule ("timestamps are an assertion, never
5	//! authoritative") applies to money exactly as it applies to the fold.
6	//!
7	//! One implementation serves both scopes: the per-tree ledger lives in the
8	//! tree's `state.sqlite`; the per-profile ledger is the same object at
9	//! `.../profiles/<profile>/ledger.sqlite`. "Reset" never deletes — it
10	//! increments the period, so the ledger is a permanent record.
